/-!
# Effectivity of formal curves: transfers along the rebasing and the rebased levels

Properties of morphisms of algebraic spaces carried along the rebasing to the integer base
(separatedness, étale charts, local finite type, quasi-compactness, dimension), the presheaf form
of properness, the representability criteria in dimension at most one, and the first part of the
tower of rebased levels of a formal object of the stack of curves (its cartesian squares, and that
each level is a separated, locally of finite type, flat algebraic space).

The file `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/CurvesFormalEffective.lean` re-exports this part. -/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing Cardinal

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

universe u v w


